{
  "id": "com.bigloude.notacmap",
  "displayName": "NOTacMap",
  "description": "Second-screen tactical map. Install it, start the game, and the map opens in your browser by itself (or open http://localhost:8123/). Drag that tab to your second monitor. A plugin inside the game reads only what your client already knows and shows your position, tracked units, airbases, incoming-missile warnings, lock lines, your marked targets and your weapon's range. FILTER and DISPLAY (top right) change what is shown and the colors. Other settings (port, auto-open, update rate) are in BepInEx/config/com.bigloude.notacmap.cfg, or in the F1 menu if you have the BepInEx Configuration Manager. Optional phone or tablet view on your home network, off by default: pick \"On another device\" when the map page asks.",
